{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Information.SkeinNPEncoding","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Information.SkeinNPEncoding","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Information.SkeinObservationBridge","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Polynomial.Eval.Degree"],"declarations":11,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.NPSkeinReduction.observed_of_accepts","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.NPSkeinReduction.observed_of_accepts","kind":"theorem","line":135,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/SkeinNPEncoding.lean#L135-L139","doc":"**Completeness of the observation as an acceptor.** Accepted instances\nare observed-halting — the converse direction of `correct`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.NPSkeinReduction.accepts_of_observed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.NPSkeinReduction.accepts_of_observed","kind":"theorem","line":128,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/SkeinNPEncoding.lean#L128-L133","doc":"**Soundness of the observation as an acceptor.** From the reduction's\ncorrectness, an observed-halting encoding forces acceptance — so a\nmatching Markov-trace observation is a *sound* accept certificate. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.NPSkeinReduction.not_uniform_polyObservable_of_superpoly","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.NPSkeinReduction.not_uniform_polyObservable_of_superpoly","kind":"theorem","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/SkeinNPEncoding.lean#L105-L126","doc":"**NP-hardness lower bound transfers to the skein observation.** If the\nencoded language admits no polynomial decision budget — for every\ncandidate polynomial budget some accepted instance escapes it (its\nsuper-polynomial lower bound) — then the skein observation is not\npoly-observable under any single polynomial budget on the encoding's\nimage. The honest QOU-internal shadow of \"the skein / Markov-trace\nobservation is NP-hard\". ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.NPSkeinReduction.decisionBudget","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.NPSkeinReduction.decisionBudget","kind":"theorem","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/SkeinNPEncoding.lean#L87-L103","doc":"**Poly-time transfer (completeness within a polynomial budget).** If\nevery accepted instance's encoding is poly-observable under a single\n`Polynomial ℕ` budget `obsBudget` (the \"P side\" on the encoding's\nimage), then each accepted instance is decided by the observation\nwithin the **genuine polynomial** `obsBudget.comp encBudget` in the\ninstance size — poly ∘ poly is poly. A poly-observable skein\nobservation collapses the encoded NP language into P. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.NPSkeinReduction.eval_mono","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.NPSkeinReduction.eval_mono","kind":"theorem","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/SkeinNPEncoding.lean#L78-L85","doc":"`Polynomial ℕ` evaluation is monotone in its argument — all\ncoefficients are `≥ 0`, so a larger input never shrinks the value. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.NPSkeinReduction.correct","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.NPSkeinReduction.correct","kind":"theorem","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/SkeinNPEncoding.lean#L71-L71","doc":"Correctness: the instance is accepted iff the encoded word is\nobserved-halting (its Markov trace matches the normal form's). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.NPSkeinReduction.enc_len_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.NPSkeinReduction.enc_len_le","kind":"theorem","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/SkeinNPEncoding.lean#L68-L68","doc":"The encoding is polynomial-size in the instance. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.NPSkeinReduction.encBudget","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.NPSkeinReduction.encBudget","kind":"def","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/SkeinNPEncoding.lean#L66-L66","doc":"The polynomial size budget of the encoding. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.NPSkeinReduction.enc","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.NPSkeinReduction.enc","kind":"def","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/SkeinNPEncoding.lean#L64-L64","doc":"Encoding of instances as skein words. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.NPSkeinReduction.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.NPSkeinReduction.mk","kind":"ctor","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/SkeinNPEncoding.lean#L61-L61","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.NPSkeinReduction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.NPSkeinReduction","kind":"structure","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/SkeinNPEncoding.lean#L55-L71","doc":"A **polynomial-size many-one reduction of a decision problem into the\nskein (Markov-trace) observation** of `sys`. Each instance `i : I` of\nsize `size i` is encoded as a skein word `enc i` whose observation\ndecides membership, at a skein length polynomial in the instance size.\nThis is the NP→Jones encoding: it witnesses that the skein observation\nis at least as hard as `accepts`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}